/-!
# Folder 156-7, pages 81–83: the supports of the two-strand string are not distributive

The finding `156-7-two-strand-supports-not-distributive` (issue
Commutator-IO/grothendieck-project#247) reads on pages 81–83 the lattice of supports of the
« ficelle à deux brins ». Its lieux are the pairs `z = (x, x')` of two chains `I`, `I'`; two
lieux are disjoint when they are comparable in the product order, `z < z'` or `z' < z`
(`Grothendieck.Folder156_7.nested`, irreflexive and symmetric). The supports are the parts equal
to the polar of their polar, `A = A^⊥⊥`; they form a complete lattice, with `A ∧ B = A ∩ B` and
`A ∨ B = (A ∪ B)^⊥⊥`, and `A_z = {z}^⊥⊥` is the support generated by `z`. For `z₁ = (x₁, x'₁)`,
`z₂ = (x₂, x'₂)` crossing and `z₃` between them, the page computes
`A_{z₃} ∧ (A_{z₁} ∨ A_{z₂}) = A_{z₃}` while `(A_{z₃} ∧ A_{z₁}) ∨ (A_{z₃} ∧ A_{z₂})` is the least
support. Folder 156-7's first file (`Grothendieck/Order/Folder156_7.lean`) proves
`z₃ ∈ {z₁, z₂}^⊥⊥` and the same computation with the singletons `{z}` in place of the `A_z`,
which are the same only when `{z}` is a support; this file takes the `A_z` themselves, in the
lattice of supports.

**What the formalisation finds.** The page's statement holds for any two chains, with `z₃`
strictly between `z₁` and `z₂` on both strands, **provided neither `z₁` nor `z₂` is an
anti-corner**: `z₁ = (x₁, x'₁)` must not have both `x₁` least in `I` and `x'₁` greatest in `I'`,
and `z₂` must not have both `x₂` greatest and `x'₂` least. Without this condition the claim is
false: in `Fin 3 × Fin 3`, with `z₁ = (0, 2)`, `z₂ = (2, 0)`, `z₃ = (1, 1)`, the lieu `z₃` lies in
`A_{z₁}` and in `A_{z₂}`, and the distributive law holds for these three supports
(`fin3_distrib_corner`). The condition holds on the page's strands `]0, 1[`, which have no least
element. Nothing else is needed: no density, no extremities, and `A_{z₃} = {z₃}` holds for any
`z₃` whose first coordinate is neither least nor greatest (`extent_lieu_eq_singleton` gives four
sufficient conditions). The edition's claim that each `A_z` of the `5 × 5` grid is `{z}` holds for
every lieu except the two anti-corners `(0, 4)` and `(4, 0)` (`fin5_extent_lieu_iff`).
« Between » is read strictly on both strands, `x₁ < x₃ < x₂` and `x'₂ < x'₃ < x'₁`. « `z < z'` »
is read as the strict product order, `z ≤ z'` and `z ≠ z'` (Mathlib's `<` on `I × I'`), as in the
edition's wording; on the `5 × 5` grid the other reading, strict on both coordinates, gives the
same failure of distributivity (`fin5_strictBoth_not_distrib`).

## Main results

* `supports_not_distrib`: for `x₁ < x₃ < x₂`, `x'₂ < x'₃ < x'₁` and `z₁`, `z₂` not anti-corners,
  `A_{z₃} ⊓ (A_{z₁} ⊔ A_{z₂}) = A_{z₃}`, `(A_{z₃} ⊓ A_{z₁}) ⊔ (A_{z₃} ⊓ A_{z₂}) = ⊥` and
  `A_{z₃} ≠ ⊥`; `not_distrib_of_between`, `not_distrib_of_noMinOrder`: the lattice of supports is
  not distributive (the second for strands without least element, the page's case);
* `mem_extent_lieu_sup_of_between`: `z₃ ∈ A_{z₁} ∨ A_{z₂}`; `extent_lieu_eq_singleton`,
  `extent_lieu_between`: `A_z = {z}`; `not_mem_extent_lieu_left`, `not_mem_extent_lieu_right`:
  `z₃ ∉ A_{z₁}`, `z₃ ∉ A_{z₂}` outside the anti-corners;
* `fin3_distrib_corner`: the anti-corner condition cannot be dropped;
* on `Fin 5 × Fin 5`, with `z₁ = (1, 3)`, `z₂ = (3, 1)`, `z₃ = (2, 2)` (the edition's own
  check, not on the page): `fin5_extent_lieu`, `fin5_extent_lieu_iff`,
  `fin5_not_orthomodular` (`A_{z₁} ≤ A_{z₁} ⊔ A_{z₂}` but
  `A_{z₁} ⊔ ((A_{z₁} ⊔ A_{z₂}) ⊓ A_{z₁}^⊥) ≠ A_{z₁} ⊔ A_{z₂}`) and `fin5_not_modular`;
  `fin5_strictBoth_not_distrib` for the other reading of `<`.

## Implementation notes

The lattice of supports is Mathlib's concept lattice `Concept X X r` (`Mathlib.Order.Concept`):
for a symmetric relation the extents of the concepts are the parts `A = A^⊥⊥`, the meet of two
concepts has the intersection for extent and the join has the closure of the union, and the
least concept has extent `∅` when `r` is irreflexive (`extent_bot_supports`). The
orthocomplement `orth` swaps extent and intent; `sup_orth` gives `c ⊔ orth c = ⊤`, so that the
failure of orthomodularity is a failure of the modular law. The `Fin` computations go through
`polarF`, the polar of a `Finset`, and are closed by `decide`.

## Not formalised

The general claim of the edition on the grids `m × n` with `m, n ≥ 2` other than `2 × 2` (neither
modular nor orthomodular) is proved only for `5 × 5`; the reading of `<` strict on both
coordinates only on that grid; and the dense case `]0, 1[ × ]0, 1[` only through
`not_distrib_of_noMinOrder` (non-distributivity), not for orthomodularity or modularity.

## References

* A. Grothendieck, *Vers une géométrie des formes*, chapter VII, « Analysis situs (troisième
  mouture) » (23–26 June 1986), Folder 156-7, pp. 81–83 (finding
  `156-7-two-strand-supports-not-distributive`)
* B. Ganter, R. Wille, *Formal Concept Analysis*, Springer, 1999 (concept lattices of a relation)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Grothendieck.Folder156_7

open Set

section Orthoset

variable {X : Type*} {r : X → X → Prop}

/-- For a symmetric relation the two polars agree. -/
theorem upperPolar_eq_lowerPolar [Std.Symm r] (s : Set X) : upperPolar r s = lowerPolar r s := by
  rw [← lowerPolar_swap, Std.Symm.swap_eq]

/-- The orthocomplement of a support: for a symmetric relation, a concept with extent and intent
swapped, i.e. the support `A^⊥`. -/
def orth [Std.Symm r] (c : Concept X X r) : Concept X X r where
  extent := c.intent
  intent := c.extent
  upperPolar_extent := by rw [← lowerPolar_swap, Std.Symm.swap_eq, c.lowerPolar_intent]
  lowerPolar_intent := by rw [← upperPolar_swap, Std.Symm.swap_eq, c.upperPolar_extent]

/-- For an irreflexive symmetric relation, `A ∨ A^⊥` is the greatest support. -/
theorem sup_orth [Std.Symm r] [Std.Irrefl r] (c : Concept X X r) : c ⊔ orth c = ⊤ :=
  Concept.ext <| by simp [orth, inter_comm c.intent, c.disjoint_extent_intent.inter_eq]

end Orthoset

section Ficelle

variable {I I' : Type*} [LinearOrder I] [LinearOrder I']

theorem nested_comm {z w : I × I'} : nested z w ↔ nested w z := Or.comm

theorem not_nested_self (z : I × I') : ¬ nested z z := by simp [nested]

instance : Std.Symm (nested (I := I) (I' := I')) := ⟨fun _ _ => Or.symm⟩

instance : Std.Irrefl (nested (I := I) (I' := I')) := ⟨not_nested_self⟩

instance : DecidableRel (nested (I := I) (I' := I')) := fun z w =>
  decidable_of_iff ((z.1 < w.1 ∧ z.2 ≤ w.2 ∨ z.1 ≤ w.1 ∧ z.2 < w.2) ∨
    (w.1 < z.1 ∧ w.2 ≤ z.2 ∨ w.1 ≤ z.1 ∧ w.2 < z.2)) (by simp only [nested, Prod.lt_iff])

variable (I I') in
/-- The lattice of supports of the two-strand string: the concepts of the relation `nested`,
whose extents are the parts `A = A^⊥⊥` of `I × I'`. -/
abbrev Supports := Concept (I × I') (I × I') nested

/-- The support `A_z = {z}^⊥⊥` generated by a lieu. -/
@[montpellier "156-7, 81–83"]
def lieu (z : I × I') : Supports I I' := Concept.ofObject nested z

theorem mem_extent_lieu {z w : I × I'} :
    w ∈ (lieu z).extent ↔ ∀ u, nested z u → nested w u := by
  simp [lieu, mem_lowerPolar_iff, mem_upperPolar_iff]

theorem mem_extent_lieu_sup_lieu {z z' w : I × I'} :
    w ∈ (lieu z ⊔ lieu z').extent ↔ ∀ u, nested z u → nested z' u → nested w u := by
  simp [lieu, mem_lowerPolar_iff, mem_upperPolar_iff]

/-- The least support is empty. -/
theorem extent_bot_supports : (⊥ : Supports I I').extent = ∅ :=
  eq_empty_iff_forall_notMem.2 fun w hw => not_nested_self w (hw (mem_univ w))

theorem not_nested_of_mem {z w : I × I'} (hw : w ∈ (lieu z).extent) : ¬ nested z w :=
  fun h => not_nested_self w (mem_extent_lieu.1 hw w h)

variable {z w : I × I'}

/-- If `z.2` is not least, the lieux of `A_z` lie to the right of `z` on the first strand. -/
theorem fst_le_of_mem (hw : w ∈ (lieu z).extent) (h : ¬ IsMin z.2) : z.1 ≤ w.1 := by
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := not_isMin_iff.1 h
  have hu : ((z.1, b) : I × I') < z := Prod.lt_iff.2 (.inr ⟨le_rfl, hb⟩)
  rcases mem_extent_lieu.1 hw _ (.inr hu) with k | k
  · exact absurd (.inr (k.trans hu)) (not_nested_of_mem hw)
  · exact (Prod.mk_le_mk.1 k.le).1

/-- If `z.2` is not greatest, the lieux of `A_z` lie to the left of `z` on the first strand. -/
theorem le_fst_of_mem (hw : w ∈ (lieu z).extent) (h : ¬ IsMax z.2) : w.1 ≤ z.1 := by
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := not_isMax_iff.1 h
  have hu : z < ((z.1, b) : I × I') := Prod.lt_iff.2 (.inr ⟨le_rfl, hb⟩)
  rcases mem_extent_lieu.1 hw _ (.inl hu) with k | k
  · exact (Prod.mk_le_mk.1 k.le).1
  · exact absurd (.inl (hu.trans k)) (not_nested_of_mem hw)

/-- If `z.1` is not least, the lieux of `A_z` lie to the right of `z` on the second strand. -/
theorem snd_le_of_mem (hw : w ∈ (lieu z).extent) (h : ¬ IsMin z.1) : z.2 ≤ w.2 := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := not_isMin_iff.1 h
  have hu : ((a, z.2) : I × I') < z := Prod.lt_iff.2 (.inl ⟨ha, le_rfl⟩)
  rcases mem_extent_lieu.1 hw _ (.inr hu) with k | k
  · exact absurd (.inr (k.trans hu)) (not_nested_of_mem hw)
  · exact (Prod.mk_le_mk.1 k.le).2

/-- If `z.1` is not greatest, the lieux of `A_z` lie to the left of `z` on the second strand. -/
theorem le_snd_of_mem (hw : w ∈ (lieu z).extent) (h : ¬ IsMax z.1) : w.2 ≤ z.2 := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := not_isMax_iff.1 h
  have hu : z < ((a, z.2) : I × I') := Prod.lt_iff.2 (.inl ⟨ha, le_rfl⟩)
  rcases mem_extent_lieu.1 hw _ (.inl hu) with k | k
  · exact (Prod.mk_le_mk.1 k.le).2
  · exact absurd (.inl (hu.trans k)) (not_nested_of_mem hw)

/-- **`A_z = {z}`**, when one coordinate of `z` is neither least nor greatest, or when neither
coordinate is least, or neither is greatest. The condition fails only near the anti-corners:
`A_{(0, 2)} ∋ (1, 1)` in `Fin 3 × Fin 3` (`ficelle_finite_not_supp`). -/
@[montpellier "156-7, 82–83"]
theorem extent_lieu_eq_singleton
    (h : ¬ IsMin z.1 ∧ ¬ IsMax z.1 ∨ ¬ IsMin z.2 ∧ ¬ IsMax z.2 ∨ ¬ IsMin z.1 ∧ ¬ IsMin z.2 ∨
      ¬ IsMax z.1 ∧ ¬ IsMax z.2) :
    (lieu z).extent = {z} := by
  refine Subset.antisymm (fun w hw => ?_) (by simp [lieu, subset_lowerPolar_upperPolar])
  suffices w ≤ z ∨ z ≤ w by
    rcases this with k | k <;> by_contra hne
    · exact not_nested_of_mem hw (.inr (k.lt_of_ne hne))
    · exact not_nested_of_mem hw (.inl (k.lt_of_ne (Ne.symm hne)))
  simp only [Prod.le_def]
  rcases h with ⟨h1, h2⟩ | ⟨h1, h2⟩ | ⟨h1, h2⟩ | ⟨h1, h2⟩
  · have := snd_le_of_mem hw h1; have := le_snd_of_mem hw h2
    rcases le_total w.1 z.1 with k | k <;> [left; right] <;> exact ⟨k, by order⟩
  · have := fst_le_of_mem hw h1; have := le_fst_of_mem hw h2
    rcases le_total w.2 z.2 with k | k <;> [left; right] <;> exact ⟨by order, k⟩
  · exact .inr ⟨fst_le_of_mem hw h2, snd_le_of_mem hw h1⟩
  · exact .inl ⟨le_fst_of_mem hw h2, le_snd_of_mem hw h1⟩

variable {x₁ x₂ x₃ : I} {y₁ y₂ y₃ : I'}

/-- **Page 83, `z₃ ∈ A_{z₁} ∨ A_{z₂}`** for `z₁ = (x₁, y₁)`, `z₂ = (x₂, y₂)` crossing and `z₃`
strictly between them on both strands; no hypothesis on the chains. -/
@[montpellier "156-7, 83"]
theorem mem_extent_lieu_sup_of_between (h13 : x₁ < x₃) (h32 : x₃ < x₂) (h23 : y₂ < y₃)
    (h31 : y₃ < y₁) : (x₃, y₃) ∈ (lieu (x₁, y₁) ⊔ lieu (x₂, y₂)).extent :=
  mem_extent_lieu_sup_lieu.2 fun u h1 h2 => ficelle_mem_supp h13 h32 h23 h31 u
    (by simpa [cosupp, nested_comm] using And.intro h1 h2)

/-- A lieu strictly between two others on the first strand generates the support `{z₃}`. -/
@[montpellier "156-7, 82–83"]
theorem extent_lieu_between (h13 : x₁ < x₃) (h32 : x₃ < x₂) :
    (lieu (x₃, y₃)).extent = {(x₃, y₃)} :=
  extent_lieu_eq_singleton (.inl ⟨not_isMin_iff.2 ⟨_, h13⟩, not_isMax_iff.2 ⟨_, h32⟩⟩)

/-- `z₃ ∉ A_{z₁}`, unless `z₁ = (x₁, y₁)` is an anti-corner (`x₁` least and `y₁` greatest). -/
@[montpellier "156-7, 83"]
theorem not_mem_extent_lieu_left (h13 : x₁ < x₃) (h31 : y₃ < y₁)
    (hz : ¬ IsMin x₁ ∨ ¬ IsMax y₁) : (x₃, y₃) ∉ (lieu (x₁, y₁)).extent := fun hw =>
  hz.elim (fun h => (snd_le_of_mem hw h).not_gt h31) fun h => (le_fst_of_mem hw h).not_gt h13

/-- `z₃ ∉ A_{z₂}`, unless `z₂ = (x₂, y₂)` is an anti-corner (`x₂` greatest and `y₂` least). -/
@[montpellier "156-7, 83"]
theorem not_mem_extent_lieu_right (h32 : x₃ < x₂) (h23 : y₂ < y₃)
    (hz : ¬ IsMax x₂ ∨ ¬ IsMin y₂) : (x₃, y₃) ∉ (lieu (x₂, y₂)).extent := fun hw =>
  hz.elim (fun h => (le_snd_of_mem hw h).not_gt h23) fun h => (fst_le_of_mem hw h).not_gt h32

theorem lieu_inf_eq_bot (h13 : x₁ < x₃) (h32 : x₃ < x₂) {z : I × I'}
    (hz : (x₃, y₃) ∉ (lieu z).extent) : lieu (x₃, y₃) ⊓ lieu z = ⊥ :=
  Concept.ext <| by
    rwa [Concept.extent_inf, extent_lieu_between h13 h32, extent_bot_supports,
      singleton_inter_eq_empty]

/-- **Pages 82–83, the computation of the page.** For `z₁ = (x₁, y₁)`, `z₂ = (x₂, y₂)` crossing,
`z₃ = (x₃, y₃)` strictly between them on both strands, and `z₁`, `z₂` not anti-corners:
`A_{z₃} ∧ (A_{z₁} ∨ A_{z₂}) = A_{z₃}`, while `(A_{z₃} ∧ A_{z₁}) ∨ (A_{z₃} ∧ A_{z₂})` is the least
support, which `A_{z₃}` is not. The anti-corner hypotheses cannot be dropped
(`fin3_distrib_corner`). -/
@[montpellier "156-7, 82–83"]
theorem supports_not_distrib (h13 : x₁ < x₃) (h32 : x₃ < x₂) (h23 : y₂ < y₃) (h31 : y₃ < y₁)
    (hz₁ : ¬ IsMin x₁ ∨ ¬ IsMax y₁) (hz₂ : ¬ IsMax x₂ ∨ ¬ IsMin y₂) :
    lieu (x₃, y₃) ⊓ (lieu (x₁, y₁) ⊔ lieu (x₂, y₂)) = lieu (x₃, y₃) ∧
      lieu (x₃, y₃) ⊓ lieu (x₁, y₁) ⊔ lieu (x₃, y₃) ⊓ lieu (x₂, y₂) = ⊥ ∧
      lieu (x₃, y₃) ≠ (⊥ : Supports I I') := by
  refine ⟨inf_eq_left.2 (Concept.ofObjects_le_iff.2 (singleton_subset_iff.2
    (mem_extent_lieu_sup_of_between h13 h32 h23 h31))), ?_, fun h => ?_⟩
  · rw [lieu_inf_eq_bot h13 h32 (not_mem_extent_lieu_left h13 h31 hz₁),
      lieu_inf_eq_bot h13 h32 (not_mem_extent_lieu_right h32 h23 hz₂), bot_sup_eq]
  · have := congrArg Concept.extent h
    rw [extent_lieu_between h13 h32, extent_bot_supports] at this
    exact singleton_ne_empty _ this

/-- **Pages 82–83, the supports of the two-strand string are not distributive**, as soon as the
strands carry three crossing lieux as in `supports_not_distrib`. -/
@[montpellier "156-7, 82–83"]
theorem not_distrib_of_between (h13 : x₁ < x₃) (h32 : x₃ < x₂) (h23 : y₂ < y₃) (h31 : y₃ < y₁)
    (hz₁ : ¬ IsMin x₁ ∨ ¬ IsMax y₁) (hz₂ : ¬ IsMax x₂ ∨ ¬ IsMin y₂) :
    ¬ ∀ a b c : Supports I I', a ⊓ (b ⊔ c) ≤ a ⊓ b ⊔ a ⊓ c := fun h => by
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3⟩ := supports_not_distrib h13 h32 h23 h31 hz₁ hz₂
  exact h3 (le_bot_iff.1 (h1 ▸ h2 ▸ h _ _ _))

/-- **The page's case**: for strands without least element (the open strands `]0, 1[`), the
supports are not distributive as soon as each strand has three elements. -/
@[montpellier "156-7, 82–83"]
theorem not_distrib_of_noMinOrder [NoMinOrder I] [NoMinOrder I'] (h13 : x₁ < x₃) (h32 : x₃ < x₂)
    (h23 : y₂ < y₃) (h31 : y₃ < y₁) :
    ¬ ∀ a b c : Supports I I', a ⊓ (b ⊔ c) ≤ a ⊓ b ⊔ a ⊓ c :=
  not_distrib_of_between h13 h32 h23 h31 (.inl (not_isMin x₁)) (.inr (not_isMin y₂))

end Ficelle

section Grids

variable {X : Type*} [Fintype X] [DecidableEq X] (r : X → X → Prop) [DecidableRel r]

/-- The polar of a `Finset`, for the computations on finite grids. -/
def polarF (S : Finset X) : Finset X := Finset.univ.filter fun x => ∀ y ∈ S, r x y

theorem coe_polarF (S : Finset X) : (polarF r S : Set X) = lowerPolar r S := by
  ext; simp [polarF, mem_lowerPolar_iff]

/-- **The anti-corner hypotheses of `supports_not_distrib` cannot be dropped.** In
`Fin 3 × Fin 3`, with `z₁ = (0, 2)`, `z₂ = (2, 0)` crossing and `z₃ = (1, 1)` between them,
`z₃ ∈ A_{z₁} ∩ A_{z₂}` and the distributive law holds for these three supports. -/
@[montpellier "156-7, 81–83"]
theorem fin3_distrib_corner :
    lieu ((1, 1) : Fin 3 × Fin 3) ⊓ (lieu (0, 2) ⊔ lieu (2, 0)) =
      lieu (1, 1) ⊓ lieu (0, 2) ⊔ lieu (1, 1) ⊓ lieu (2, 0) := by
  have h : ∀ z : Fin 3 × Fin 3, z ∈ ({(0, 2), (2, 0)} : Set _) →
      lieu ((1, 1) : Fin 3 × Fin 3) ≤ lieu z := by
    rintro z (rfl | rfl) <;>
    exact Concept.ofObjects_le_iff.2 (singleton_subset_iff.2 (mem_extent_lieu.2 (by decide)))
  rw [inf_eq_left.2 (h _ (by simp)), inf_eq_left.2 (h _ (by simp)), sup_idem,
    inf_eq_left.2 ((h _ (by simp)).trans le_sup_left)]

/-- The edition's check on the `5 × 5` grid: `A_z = {z}` for `z₁ = (1, 3)`, `z₂ = (3, 1)` and
`z₃ = (2, 2)`. -/
@[montpellier "156-7, 81–83"]
theorem fin5_extent_lieu :
    (lieu ((1, 3) : Fin 5 × Fin 5)).extent = {(1, 3)} ∧
      (lieu ((3, 1) : Fin 5 × Fin 5)).extent = {(3, 1)} ∧
      (lieu ((2, 2) : Fin 5 × Fin 5)).extent = {(2, 2)} := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩ <;> exact extent_lieu_eq_singleton (.inl ⟨not_isMin_iff.2 ⟨0, by decide⟩,
    not_isMax_iff.2 ⟨4, by decide⟩⟩)

/-- On the `5 × 5` grid, `A_z = {z}` for every lieu except the two anti-corners `(0, 4)` and
`(4, 0)`. -/
@[montpellier "156-7, 81–83"]
theorem fin5_extent_lieu_iff (z : Fin 5 × Fin 5) :
    (lieu z).extent = {z} ↔ z ≠ (0, 4) ∧ z ≠ (4, 0) := by
  simp only [lieu, Concept.extent_ofObjects, upperPolar_eq_lowerPolar, ← Finset.coe_singleton,
    ← coe_polarF, Finset.coe_inj]
  revert z
  decide

/-- **The edition's check on the `5 × 5` grid: the supports are not orthomodular.** For
`z₁ = (1, 3)`, `z₂ = (3, 1)`: `A_{z₁} ≤ A_{z₁} ∨ A_{z₂}`, but
`A_{z₁} ∨ ((A_{z₁} ∨ A_{z₂}) ∧ A_{z₁}^⊥) ≠ A_{z₁} ∨ A_{z₂}`. -/
@[montpellier "156-7, 81–83"]
theorem fin5_not_orthomodular :
    lieu ((1, 3) : Fin 5 × Fin 5) ≤ lieu (1, 3) ⊔ lieu (3, 1) ∧
      lieu (1, 3) ⊔ (lieu (1, 3) ⊔ lieu (3, 1)) ⊓ orth (lieu ((1, 3) : Fin 5 × Fin 5)) ≠
        lieu (1, 3) ⊔ lieu (3, 1) := by
  refine ⟨le_sup_left, fun h => ?_⟩
  have := congrArg Concept.extent h
  simp only [Concept.extent_sup, Concept.intent_inf, orth, lieu, Concept.intent_ofObjects,
    Concept.extent_ofObjects, upperPolar_eq_lowerPolar, ← Finset.coe_singleton, ← coe_polarF,
    ← Finset.coe_inter, Finset.coe_inj] at this
  revert this
  decide

/-- **The supports of the `5 × 5` grid are not modular**: the modular law applied to `A_{z₁}`,
`A_{z₁}^⊥` and `A_{z₁} ∨ A_{z₂}` would give the orthomodular law refuted in
`fin5_not_orthomodular`, since `A_{z₁} ∨ A_{z₁}^⊥` is the greatest support. -/
@[montpellier "156-7, 81–83"]
theorem fin5_not_modular : ¬ IsModularLattice (Supports (Fin 5) (Fin 5)) := fun h => by
  obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := fin5_not_orthomodular
  refine h2 (le_antisymm (sup_le h1 inf_le_left) ?_)
  have := h.sup_inf_le_assoc_of_le (orth (lieu ((1, 3) : Fin 5 × Fin 5))) h1
  rwa [sup_orth, top_inf_eq, inf_comm] at this

/-- The other reading of « `z < z'` »: strictly smaller on both coordinates. -/
def strictBoth (z w : Fin 5 × Fin 5) : Prop :=
  z.1 < w.1 ∧ z.2 < w.2 ∨ w.1 < z.1 ∧ w.2 < z.2

instance : DecidableRel strictBoth := fun _ _ => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (_ ∨ _))

instance : Std.Symm strictBoth := ⟨fun _ _ => Or.symm⟩

/-- With disjointness read as strict comparability on both coordinates, the same three lieux of
the `5 × 5` grid refute distributivity in the same way. -/
@[montpellier "156-7, 81–83"]
theorem fin5_strictBoth_not_distrib :
    Concept.ofObject strictBoth (2, 2) ⊓
        (Concept.ofObject strictBoth (1, 3) ⊔ Concept.ofObject strictBoth (3, 1)) =
      Concept.ofObject strictBoth (2, 2) ∧
    Concept.ofObject strictBoth (2, 2) ⊓ Concept.ofObject strictBoth (1, 3) ⊔
        Concept.ofObject strictBoth (2, 2) ⊓ Concept.ofObject strictBoth (3, 1) = ⊥ := by
  constructor <;> refine Concept.ext ?_ <;>
  simp only [Concept.extent_sup, Concept.extent_inf, Concept.intent_inf, Concept.extent_bot,
    Concept.extent_ofObjects, Concept.intent_ofObjects, upperPolar_eq_lowerPolar,
    ← Finset.coe_singleton, ← coe_polarF, ← Finset.coe_inter, ← Finset.coe_univ,
    Finset.coe_inj] <;>
  decide

end Grids

